 "notes": {
  "ktx2": "Not done. KTX2 (KHR_texture_basisu, ETC1S or UASTC, transcoded in the browser by three's KTX2Loader + basis_transcoder.wasm) would keep textures compressed on the GPU: about 4-8x less GPU memory than RGBA8 WebP (ETC1S ~0.5-1 byte/texel), so the 2048 atlases could come back within budget and phones would drop to ~5 MB. Costs: the transcoder (~0.5 MB wasm) and its setup, slower first upload, ETC1S blockiness in the dark gradients (UASTC avoids it at ~2x the download). /opt/homebrew/bin/basisu exists on this machine, so it needs no install.",
  "viewer": "_dev/room/room.glb (with the baked armillary) is unchanged for sketches/room/."
 }
